# Section width vs navbar

The navbar is an inset pill: `max-w-[1301px]` with `lg:px-10`. Content sections must **protrude a bit past the navbar**, not sit narrower than it.

- Wrap page sections (heroes, cards, CTAs, technical blocks) in `SectionContainer` from `@/components/ui/layout`.
- `SectionContainer` is `max-w-[1366px]` with `px-3 sm:px-5 lg:px-0`.
- Do **not** wrap those blocks in `PageContainer` (`lg:px-[56px]` makes them narrower than the nav).
- Use `PageContainer` only for small inset chrome such as back links.
- Do not make the navbar full-bleed to match content. Keep the pill inset; make sections wider.
- **Exception — crear cuenta / recuperar clave:** compact and centered (`max-w-[760px]`). Do not stretch them to `SectionContainer`.
- **Exception — iniciar sesión:** compact centered split (`max-w-[420px]` on mobile, `max-w-[920px]` on desktop). Do not stretch it to `1366px` or full viewport height.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — section ends up narrower than the navbar
<PageContainer>
  <DetailHero />
</PageContainer>

// ✅ GOOD
<PageContainer>
  <Link href="...">Volver</Link>
</PageContainer>
<SectionContainer>
  <DetailHero />
</SectionContainer>
```
